## 16. The projective tranche: cancellation *before* majorization

The envelope of item 15 takes absolute values radius by radius,

    |R(2r)A₀(r) − R(r)A₀(2r)| ≤ |R(2r)||A₀(r)| + |R(r)||A₀(2r)|,

and therefore discards the two-radius cancellation the literal balance actually
constrains.  This tranche replaces it.  For any scalar channel `C` put

    𝔇_C(r) = C(2r) A₀(r) − C(r) A₀(2r).

* `LiteralWeilProjectiveResidualDecomposition` — the exact channel-by-channel
  determinant decomposition `𝔇_R = 𝔇_{Z_off} + 𝔇_P + 𝔇_Γ + 𝔇_Π`
  (`residualProjectiveDecomposition`), proved by linearity, together with
  `primeProjectiveDefect = 0` in the short-taper lane and the resulting
  `clusterHeightDefect_eq_threeProjectiveChannels`.

* `LiteralWeilProjectiveTaper` — the two-radius bracket
  `B_r(u) = A₀(r) cos(2ru) − A₀(2r) cos(ru)` and the projective taper
  `h_r = g · B_r`.  Every channel that is a cosine transform in the sampling
  radius has its projective defect equal to that same channel evaluated at radius
  `0` with taper `h_r`.  The bracket and its first two derivatives are all
  `O(r²)`: `|B_r| ≤ 5r²Λ²‖g‖₁`, `|B_r′| ≤ 5r²Λ‖g‖₁`, `|B_r″| ≤ 5r²‖g‖₁`.

* `LiteralWeilProjectiveStripConstant` — consequently
  `stripConst (sampleTest h_r t 0) Λ ≤ r² · projStripCoeff g Λ t`
  (`stripConst_projTaper_le`), and hence
  `|𝔇_{Z_off}| ≤ r² · 4 · projStripCoeff · W(t)` (`offOrdProjectiveTailQuadratic`).

* `LiteralWeilGammaProjectiveBound` — the exact identity
  `𝔇_Γ = −2 · gammaResp h_r t 0` (`gammaProjectiveDefect_eq`) and an absolute
  constant `C_Γ ≥ 0` with `|𝔇_Γ| ≤ r² · projStripCoeff · C_Γ`.

* `LiteralWeilPoleProjectiveCancellation` — **deliberate deviation from the
  suggested target.**  An exact `𝔇_Π = 0` was *not* pursued as a taper
  constraint: within the two-bump positive family already in the repository the
  relevant quadratic in the mixing parameter has no sign change, so no
  intermediate-value root exists and the collinearity condition
  `P_t(2r)/P_t(r) = A₀(2r)/A₀(r)` cannot be met there.  What is proved instead is
  strictly stronger for the purpose at hand, because it needs no side condition:
  `|𝔇_Π| ≤ 20 r² Λ² cosh(Λ/2) ‖g‖₁²` unconditionally
  (`abs_poleProjectiveDefect_le'`).

* `LiteralWeilProjectiveSeparationGate` — the assembled envelope
  `|D_cluster(t,r)| ≤ r² · E_proj(g, Λ, t, C_Γ)` (`exists_projectiveEnvelope`) with
  `E_proj` independent of `r`, and the capstone sandwich
  `0 < D_{ρ*}(r) ≤ D_cluster(t,r) ≤ r² · E_proj`
  (`targetZeroDefect_le_projectiveEnvelope`).

This is a genuine order improvement: the old envelope was `O(1)` as `r → 0`, the
projectivized one is `O(r²)`.

## 17. The signal side at the same order, and the exact remaining obligation

`LiteralWeilTargetDefectLeadingCoefficient` puts the signal on the same footing.
With `M_y = ∫ g cosh(yu)`, `N_y = ∫ g u² cosh(yu)`:

* `abs_cos_sub_quadratic_le` — the *global* bound `|cos x − (1 − x²/2)| ≤ x⁴/24`,
  proved here from scratch (Mathlib's `Real.cos_bound` is restricted to `|x| ≤ 1`);
* `abs_evenResp_sub_quadratic_le` — `|A_y(s) − (M_y − s²N_y/2)| ≤ (s⁴/24) Q⁴_y`;
* `abs_heightDefect_sub_leading_le` — for `0 ≤ r ≤ 1`,

      |heightDefect(g, r, a, 0) − r² · (3/2)(N_a M_0 − M_a N_0)|
        ≤ r⁴ · defectRemainderCoeff(g, a);

* `gate_of_coefficientComparison` — the gate inequality `r² E < D_ρ(r)` follows
  from the **radius-free** comparison

      E + r² · zeroRemainderCoeff(g, ρ)  <  zeroLeadingCoeff(g, ρ)
        = 2 m_ρ · (3/2)(N_a M_0 − M_a N_0),   a = heightOf ρ.

So the frontier has moved from an order mismatch to a coefficient comparison.

### The first unproved theorem, stated exactly

> For an actual nontrivial zero `ρ* = 1/2 + a + it` of `riemannZeta` with `a ≠ 0`,
> `t ≠ 0`, `9π ≤ 4|t| log 2`, and gate data `GateData g t r Λ` produced by
> `exists_gateData` (so `Λ = 9π/(4|t|)`), with `C_Γ` the constant of
> `exists_gammaProjectiveEnvelope`:
>
>     r² · projectiveEnvelope g Λ t C_Γ  <  zeroHeightDefect g r ρ*.
>
> Equivalently, by `gate_of_coefficientComparison`, it suffices to prove the
> radius-free comparison
>
>     projectiveEnvelope g Λ t C_Γ + r² · zeroRemainderCoeff g ρ*
>       < zeroLeadingCoeff g ρ*.

This inequality is a hypothesis in `false_of_projectiveEnvelope_lt_targetDefect`,
`no_offLineZero_of_projectiveEnvelope_lt_targetDefect` and
`gate_of_coefficientComparison`; it is never asserted anywhere in the development.
`RiemannHypothesisFor` is not weakened and is not derived.

